refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
public boolintZipArchive::openString stringdata"" intflags0
Opens a ZIP archive whose contents are held in a string, instead of in a file. Called without arguments, it starts a new, empty archive in memory. Use ZipArchive::closeString to get the resulting archive back as a string.

  &reftitle.examples;

   Creating an archive in memory


<?php
$zip = new ZipArchive;
$zip->openString();
$zip->addFromString('hello.txt', "Hello\n");
$bytes = $zip->closeString();

// $bytes can be sent to a client or stored, and read back later.
$zip = new ZipArchive;
var_dump($zip->openString($bytes));
var_dump($zip->getFromName('hello.txt'));
?>


   &example.outputs;


bool(true)
string(6) "Hello
